nt_id":"MCTM-049493","value":"10.49","numeric":10.49}},{"Measurement_ID":"MCTM-051808","Abbreviation_in_the_article":"DN604","Cell_line":"SGC-7901","Time(h)":72,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":5.13,"IC50_Dark_value":5.13,"Method":"MTT","DOI":"10.1124/jpet.117.243451","Year":2017,"Type":"IC50","comparison":{"compound_id":"OBMD011700","measurement_id":"MCTM-051808","value":"1.73","numeric":1.73}},{"Measurement_ID":"MCTM-051809","Abbreviation_in_the_article":"DN604","Cell_line":"SGC-7901/DDP","Time(h)":72,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":5.09,"IC50_Dark_value":5.09,"Method":"MTT","DOI":"10.1124/jpet.117.243451","Year":2017,"Type":"IC50","comparison":{"compound_id":"OBMD011700","measurement_id":"MCTM-051809","value":"12.26","numeric":12.26}},{"Measurement_ID":"MCTM-051810","Abbreviation_in_the_article":"DN604","Cell_line":"A549","Time(h)":72,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":4.59,"IC50_Dark_value":4.59,"Method":"MTT","DOI":"10.1124/jpet.117.243451","Year":2017,"Type":"IC50","comparison":{"compound_id":"OBMD011700","measurement_id":"MCTM-051810","value":"2.06","numeric":2.06}},{"Measurement_ID":"MCTM-051811","Abbreviation_in_the_article":"DN604","Cell_line":"A549cisR","Time(h)":72,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":4.01,"IC50_Dark_value":4.01,"Method":"MTT","DOI":"10.1124/jpet.117.243451","Year":2017,"Type":"IC50","comparison":{"compound_id":"OBMD011700","measurement_id":"MCTM-051811","value":"19.75","numeric":19.75}},{"Measurement_ID":"MCTM-051812","Abbreviation_in_the_article":"DN604","Cell_line":"HUVEC","Time(h)":72,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":30.85,"IC50_Dark_value":30.85,"Method":"MTT","DOI":"10.1124/jpet.117.243451","Year":2017,"Type":"IC50","comparison":{"compound_id":"OBMD011700","measurement_id":"MCTM-051812","value":"10.35","numeric":10.35}}],"logp":[{"abbreviation_in_the_article":"DN604","value":-1.17,"value_relation":"=","type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"100 mM phosphate buffer","pH":7.4,"temperature_C":37,"doi":"10.1002/chem.201404090","year":2014,"record_id":"MLDB-002032","detection":"HPLC","method_description":"The log Pow determination of DN604 was conducted by using the shake flask method. Excess DN604 was dissolved in KH2PO4/NaOH (0.1 M, pH 7.4) buffer solution presaturated with n-octanol for 48 h at 37 °C. The solution was filtered to remove undissolved platinum(II) compound. The initial concentration of platinum content was determined by RP-HPLC analysis. Subsequently, the platinum(II) solution was added to an equal volume of n-octanol (presaturated with KH2PO4/NaOH buffer for 48 h). The heterogeneous mixture was shaken vigorously for 2 h before centrifuging for 15 min to achieve phase separation. The final concentration of platinum content in the aqueous phase was again determined by RP-HPLC, and the water–octanol partition coefficient was calculated. In addition, all the aqueous solution was diluted 10 fold before HPLC study due to the high concentration. The experiment was performed in triplicate."},{"abbreviation_in_the_article":"DN604","value":-2.1,"value_relation":"=","std":0.2,"type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"water","doi":"10.1016/j.bioorg.2020.104210","year":2020,"record_id":"MLDB-002071","detection":"ICP-MS","method_description":"In a n-octanol/water system, the lipophilicity of cisplatin, DN604, C1, and C2 was measured by a shake flask method. An aqueous solution (1.0 mL) of several compounds of equal concentration was mixed with n-octanol, centrifuged at room temperature for 4 h, centrifuged at 2500 rpm, and centrifuged for 15 min to separate the different phases. The solutes in the liquid phase were separated and the platinum content in the initial and final phases was determined by ICP-MS. The log PO/W was calculated using the following equation: log PO/W = log [(Ptinitial - Ptfinal)/ Ptfinal]"}]}